<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="margin: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="text-align: right; margin: 0"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="margin: 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>Bit Origin Ltd Announces 1-for-60 Reverse Stock
Split Effective January&nbsp;20, 2026</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white"><B>SINGAPORE, January&nbsp;15, 2026 (GLOBE
NEWSWIRE)</B> &mdash; Bit Origin Ltd (NASDAQ: BTOG) (&ldquo;Bit Origin&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;), today announced that its
Board of Directors has approved a 1-for-60 reverse stock split of the Company&rsquo;s Class&nbsp;A ordinary shares and Class&nbsp;B ordinary
shares (the &ldquo;Reverse Stock Split&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">Beginning with the opening of trading on January&nbsp;20,
2026, the Company&rsquo;s Class&nbsp;A ordinary shares will trade on the Nasdaq Capital Market on a reverse-split-adjusted basis under
the existing ticker symbol &ldquo;BTOG.&rdquo; The new CUSIP number of the Company&rsquo;s Class&nbsp;A ordinary shares will be G21621134.When
the Reverse Stock Split becomes effective, every sixty (60) issued and outstanding Class&nbsp;A ordinary shares will be automatically
combined into one (1)&nbsp;Class&nbsp;A ordinary share, and every sixty (60) issued and outstanding Class&nbsp;B ordinary shares will
be automatically combined into one (1)&nbsp;Class&nbsp;B ordinary share.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">&ldquo;The reverse stock split is intended
to support our efforts to maintain compliance with Nasdaq&rsquo;s minimum bid price requirement under Nasdaq Listing Rule&nbsp;5550(a)(2),&rdquo;
said Jinghai Jiang, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Bit Origin. &ldquo;While the Reverse Stock Split is intended to assist the
Company in regaining compliance with Nasdaq Listing Rule&nbsp;5550(a)(2), the Company cannot assure that it will be able to regain or
maintain compliance with Nasdaq&rsquo;s continued listing standards. We remain focused on executing our strategic initiatives and enhancing
long-term value for our shareholders.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">As a result of the Reverse Stock Split, the
number of outstanding Class&nbsp;A ordinary shares of Bit Origin will be reduced from approximately 88.6 million to approximately 1.5
million and the number of outstanding Class&nbsp;B ordinary shares of Bit Origin will be reduced from 768,000 to 12,800 shares. Concurrently
with the reverse stock split, the Company amended its Memorandum of Association to proportionately reduce the number of authorized ordinary
for issuance and change the par value of post-reverse stock split ordinary shares to $0.00006 per shareAll outstanding options, warrants
and other securities entitling holders to purchase or receive ordinary shares will be adjusted in accordance with their respective terms.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">No fractional shares will be issued in connection
with the Reverse Stock Split. Shareholders who would otherwise be entitled to receive fractional shares will receive one full share.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white"><B>About Bit Origin Ltd</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white">Bit Origin Ltd (NASDAQ: BTOG) is an emerging growth company focused on digital asset innovation and blockchain-based strategies, including
the development of its digital asset treasury initiatives and related ecosystem opportunities. For more information, please visit <U>https://bitorigin.io</U>.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"></P>

